{'review': '{\n  "review": "<<<ARTIFACT review_report>>>\\n{\\n  \\"overall_status\\": \\"NEEDS_FIXES\\",\\n  \\"quality_score\\": 6.5,\\n  \\"summary\\": {\\n    \\"critical\\": 0,\\n    \\"high\\": 2,\\n    \\"medium\\": 2,\\n    \\"low\\": 1,\\n    \\"passed_checks\\": [\\"No hardcoded secrets\\", \\"Tests follow AAA pattern\\", \\"Distinct test data prevents interference\\"]\\n  },\\n  \\"findings\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-001\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"high\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"HttpClient not disposed causing potential resource leaks\\",\\n      \\"file\\": \\"tests/Api.Tests/AuthEndpointsTests.cs\\",\\n      \\"line_range\\": [23, 23],\\n      \\"description\\": "Each test creates an HttpClient via _factory.CreateClient() but never disposes it. While the test process is short-lived, this pattern can lead to socket exhaustion in large test suites or long-running test processes.",\\n      "impact": "Potential socket exhaustion and increased memory usage during test execution, especially in CI/CD pipelines with parallel test runs.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Wrap the HttpClient in a using statement to ensure proper disposal.",\\n      "code_before": "            var client = _factory.CreateClient();\\n            var request = new RegisterRequest(\\"testuser\\", \\"test@example.com\\", \\"Password123!\\");\\n\\n            // Act\\n            var response = await client.PostAsJsonAsync(\\"/v1/auth/register\\", request);",\\n      "code_after": "            using var client = _factory.CreateClient();\\n            var request = new RegisterRequest(\\"testuser\\", \\"test@example.com\\", \\"Password123!\\");\\n\\n            // Act\\n            var response = await client.PostAsJsonAsync(\\"/v1/auth/register\\", request);",\\n      "references": ["Microsoft Docs: HttpClient disposal", "CA2000"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"finding_id\\": \\"F-002\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"high\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"Use of dynamic type for error response reduces test maintainability\\",\\n      \\"file\\": \\"tests/Api.Tests/AuthEndpointsTests.cs\\",\\n      \\"line_range\\": [40, 40],\\n      "description": "The tests use dynamic to parse error responses (e.g., var error = await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<dynamic>();). This lacks compile-time safety and makes tests brittle to response structure changes.",\\n      "impact": "Tests may fail unexpectedly if the error response shape changes (e.g., adding nested properties), requiring manual updates rather than compiler-assisted refactoring.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Define a strongly-typed error response class (e.g., ApiError) and use it for deserialization.",\\n      "code_before": "            var error = await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<dynamic>();\\n            Assert.Equal(\\"Username already exists.\\", (string)error!.error);",\\n      "code_after": "            var error = await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ApiError>();\\n            Assert.Equal(\\"Username already exists.\\", error.Error);",\\n      "references": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      "finding_id\\": \\"F-003\\",\\n      \\"severity\\": \\"medium\\",\\n      \\"category\\": \\"quality\\",\\n      \\"title\\": \\"Missing test for login with existing user but wrong password\\",\\n      \\"file\\": \\"tests/Api.Tests/AuthEndpointsTests.cs\\",\\n      \\"line_range\\": [78, 90],\\n      "description": "The Login_InvalidCredentials_ReturnsUnauthorized test only covers non-existent users. It does not verify the system\'s response when an existing user provides an incorrect password.",\\n      "impact": "Missing test coverage for a common authentication failure scenario, potentially allowing regressions in password validation logic to go undetected.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Add a test case that registers a user, then attempts login with the correct username but incorrect password.",\\n      "code_before": "        [Fact]\\n        public async Task Login_InvalidCredentials_ReturnsUnauthorized()\\n        {\\n            // Arrange\\n            var client = _factory.CreateClient();\\n            var loginRequest = new LoginRequest(\\"nonexistent\\", \\"wrongpassword\\");\\n\\n            // Act\\n            var response = await client.PostAsJsonAsync(\\"/v1/auth/login\\", loginRequest);\\n\\n            // Assert\\n            Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.Unauthorized, response.StatusCode);\\n            var error = await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<dynamic>();\\n            Assert.Equal(\\"Invalid username or password.\\", (string)error!.error);\\n        }",\\n      "code_after": "        [Fact]\\n        public async Task Login_InvalidCredentials_ReturnsUnauthorized()\\n        {\\n            // Arrange\\n            var client = _factory.CreateClient();\\n            var loginRequest = new LoginRequest(\\"nonexistent\\", \\"wrongpassword\\");\\n\\n            // Act\\n            var response = await client.PostAsJsonAsync(\\"/v1/auth/login\\", loginRequest);\\n\\n            // Assert\\n            Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.Unauthorized, response.StatusCode);\\n            var error = await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ApiError>();\\n            Assert.Equal(\\"Invalid username or password.\\", error.Error);\\n        }\\n\\n        [Fact]\\n        public async Task Login_ExistingUserWrongPassword_ReturnsUnauthorized()\\n        {\\n            // Arrange\\n            var client = _factory.CreateClient();\\n            var registerRequest = new RegisterRequest(\\"wrongpassuser\\", \\"wrongpass@example.com\\", \\"Password123!\\");\\n            await client.PostAsJsonAsync(\\"/v1/auth/register\\", registerRequest);\\n\\n            var loginRequest = new LoginRequest(\\"wrongpassuser\\", \\"WrongPassword456@\\");\\n\\n            // Act\\n            var response = await client.PostAsJsonAsync(\\"/v1/auth/login\\", loginRequest);\\n\\n            // Assert\\n            Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.Unauthorized, response.StatusCode);\\n            var error = await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ApiError>();\\n            Assert.Equal(\\"Invalid username or password.\\", error.Error);\\n        }",\\n      "references": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      "finding_id\\": \\"F-004\\",\\n      "severity": "medium",\\n      "category": "quality",\\n      "title": "Missing validation tests for malformed register/login requests",\\n      "file": "tests/Api.Tests/AuthEndpointsTests.cs",\\n      "line_range": [23, 90],\\n      "description": "The test suite does not include tests for invalid input formats (e.g., missing fields, invalid email, weak password) that should return 400 Bad Request via model validation.",\\n      "impact": "Missing test coverage for input validation could allow regressions in request model validation or API validation logic to reach production.",\\n      "suggested_fix": "Add test cases for:\\n- Register with missing username\\n- Register with invalid email format\\n- Register with password missing complexity requirements\\n- Login with empty username/password",\\n      "code_before": "",\\n      "code_after": "        [Fact]\\n        public async Task Register_MissingUsername_ReturnsBadRequest()\\n        {\\n            // Arrange\\n            var client = _factory.CreateClient();\\n            var request = new RegisterRequest(null, \\"test@example.com\\", \\"Password123!\\");\\n\\n            // Act\\n            var response = await client.PostAsJsonAsync(\\"/v1/auth/register\\", request);\\n\\n            // Assert\\n            Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.BadRequest, response.StatusCode);\\n            // Additional assertions on validation errors\\n        }\\n\\n        // Similar tests for invalid email, weak password, etc.",\\n      "references": []\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  "positive_observations": [\\n    \\"Tests use unique usernames/emails to prevent test interference\\",\\n    \\"Both success and failure paths are tested for core scenarios\\",\\n    \\"Async/await is used correctly throughout\\",\\n    \\"Arrange-Act-Act-Assert pattern is followed clearly\\",\\n    \\"Token presence and username are validated in success cases\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n<<<ENDARTIFACT>>>\\n"\n}'}